<%# Reports index (module 8 part 8.3).
    The sidebar's Reports group points HERE rather than at a single report, so adding the
    module's later reports (forecast, variance, portfolio) does not require re-pointing the
    link — and the sidebar-contract test (MS6.8) keeps working because the route it names
    already exists.

    One report exists today: Receivables aging. It is listed first because PRD §5.2 calls it
    "Finance's collection priority list" — the screen Finance opens every morning.

    Title and sub-title come from `page()` in routes/reporting.js. %>
<% if (typeof project === 'undefined' || !project) { %>
<div class="card"><div class="fbody">
  <p class="dim">No project is in scope for your account, so there are no reports to show.</p>
</div></div>
<% } else { %>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-hd"><h2>Available reports</h2>
    <span class="r"><%= total %> claim<%= total === 1 ? '' : 's' %> outstanding</span></div>
  <div class="tw"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Report</th><th>What it answers</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/reports/aging"><b>Receivables aging</b></a></td>
        <td>Who owes us money, how late it is, and which invoices are past their terms.</td>
      </tr>
      <%# Module 8 part 8.4. Listed here rather than re-pointing the sidebar, which is the
          whole reason this index exists. %>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/reports/forecast"><b>Cost forecast</b></a></td>
        <td>What the project is likely to finally cost — the arithmetic estimate and the
          Cost Controller's own forecast, side by side.</td>
      </tr>
      <%# Module 8 part 8.5. %>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/reports/variance"><b>Variance</b></a></td>
        <td>Whether the project is ahead of or behind the plan, and by how much in rupiah.</td>
      </tr>
      <%# Module 8 part 8.8: revenue recognition (PRD §5.3). %>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/reports/revenue"><b>Revenue recognition</b></a></td>
        <td>What has been earned under the project's revenue method, and the difference between
          what is recognised, invoiced and received.</td>
      </tr>
      <%# Module 8 part 8.10: the monthly Project Update Report (PRD §5.4). Listed FIRST among the
          month-end reports because it is the artefact the whole month closes on — approving it
          freezes the period. %>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/reports/update"><b>Project update report</b></a></td>
        <td>The month's position: schedule and cost performance, receivable against recognised
          revenue, payable, the exceptions, and what changed in the baseline. Approving it
          freezes the period.</td>
      </tr>
      <%# Module 8 part 8.6. %>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/reports/project"><b>Project overview</b></a></td>
        <td>Planned, earned and actual cost month by month — the S-curves, and the estimate at
          completion.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</div>

<div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));margin-top:12px">
  <% tiles.forEach(function(t){ %>
  <div class="card kpi">
    <div class="lbl"><%= t.label %></div>
    <div class="v mono sm"><%= fmt(t.total) %></div>
    <div class="f"><%= t.n %> claim<%= t.n === 1 ? '' : 's' %></div>
  </div>
  <% }); %>
</div>

<% } %>
